1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,586
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:08,466
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,719
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,518
[Emerson] <i>What's that? Atomic bomb?</i>

7
00:00:18,601 --> 00:00:21,187
[Paldo] <i>That's a bazooka!</i>
<i>Avoid it, or we'll be dust!</i>

8
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:22,772
[Atoy] Okay, okay, okay! I'll go to you!

9
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:24,399
[whooshes, then explosion]

10
00:00:24,482 --> 00:00:25,483
PREVIOUSLY

11
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:26,693
- [grunts]
- [tires screeching]

12
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:30,363
[Paldo] <i>You need to make sure you live!</i>
<i>You need to tell Atoy the truth!</i>

13
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:31,281
What truth?!

14
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:33,533
[grunts, groans]

15
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:39,164
It's about your father.

16
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:41,750
[Paldo] <i>The day your father</i>
<i>got hit-and-run,</i>

17
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:43,293
<i>you were really the target</i>

18
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:45,211
<i>because you compromised</i>
<i>the shipment at the port.</i>

19
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:46,921
You ran over my father?

20
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:48,423
[Paldo gasps] <i>Not me.</i>

21
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:50,467
- [Atoy] <i>Who?</i>
- [Paldo] <i>Red.</i>

22
00:00:51,926 --> 00:00:53,219
[explosion]

23
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:55,555
[Mongki] <i>Boss, Paldo escaped.</i>

24
00:00:55,638 --> 00:00:57,223
[Red] <i>Where does Paldo live?</i>
<i>Let's visit him.</i>

25
00:00:57,807 --> 00:00:59,684
[Atoy] All this time,
the people who killed my father

26
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:00,977
are the ones we deal with!

27
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,937
Are you also looking for Paldo?

28
00:01:03,021 --> 00:01:04,898
[Nestor] <i>I've been calling,</i>
<i>but no one's answering.</i>

29
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:07,776
Atoy always asks me about you.

30
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:10,028
He's sad that you're ignoring him.

31
00:01:10,111 --> 00:01:11,404
You're just saying that.

32
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:12,739
[car revving]

33
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:16,076
Ibyang! Help!

34
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,577
[Munggo] <i>She was taken to the hospital!</i>

35
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,954
- She almost got run over earlier!
- [Ame] Huh?

36
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:21,414
Let's make up now.

37
00:01:21,498 --> 00:01:23,124
It's just you who's mad at me.

38
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:24,167
[Atoy] <i>It's just you, really.</i>

39
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:25,585
[Emerson] <i>It's a blessing in disguise.</i>

40
00:01:25,668 --> 00:01:28,296
<i>Think about it.</i>
<i>Had you rushed to confront Red earlier,</i>

41
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:29,672
<i>you probably would have been killed there.</i>

42
00:01:30,298 --> 00:01:31,758
He's lucky

43
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:35,678
because he'll still make
it until tomorrow.

44
00:01:38,765 --> 00:01:39,849
[music fades]

45
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:41,267
[cool upbeat music playing]

46
00:01:41,351 --> 00:01:43,478
[giggling, indistinct chattering]

47
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:45,230
[Jona] What's yours?
I've been here a while.

48
00:01:45,313 --> 00:01:47,690
- [Mona] Mona.
- [Jona] Hi, I'm Jona.

49
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:50,485
[Jona] Hello! He smiled!

50
00:01:50,568 --> 00:01:52,487
He's missing a tooth. But it's fine.

51
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:53,780
- [overlapping chatter]
- [in English] Excuse me.

52
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:54,823
Oh.

53
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:56,825
You were with Karla earlier, right?

54
00:01:56,908 --> 00:01:58,159
Which one of you is Denden?

55
00:01:58,243 --> 00:01:59,869
- Den--
- Ah, Denden.

56
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:00,995
She already went home.

57
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:04,749
She suddenly saw her ex,
so, she hurriedly left.

58
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:06,709
[Mona] But you're Gavin, right?

59
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:08,044
Karla's friend.

60
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:09,295
Oh my gosh, it's him!

61
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:10,797
Take care of Karla, okay.

62
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:12,257
We're moving to other guys!

63
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,424
Yes, yes. Ah--

64
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:15,051
[Jona] Bring her home safe, okay?

65
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:17,345
- Or else, Brother Atoy will be mad!
- [Mona] Yes.

66
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:19,180
- [Jona] He'll be mad. Oh, take care…
- Okay, fine.

67
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:21,015
- [Jona] Bye.
- So, Be? We're leaving.

68
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:22,934
Let's go. Bye, handsome!

69
00:02:23,017 --> 00:02:25,019
He's following us.

70
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:26,396
[Jona] Don't follow us.

71
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:27,730
[Jona exclaims]

72
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:30,400
[Cathy] Karla, go. Go on.

73
00:02:30,483 --> 00:02:31,568
[in English] Make friends. Have fun!

74
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:37,532
- [cool upbeat music playing]
- [lively chatter]

75
00:02:37,615 --> 00:02:39,868
[in English] Have fun! [chuckles]

76
00:02:40,743 --> 00:02:41,953
[Cathy] Let her.

77
00:02:42,036 --> 00:02:45,248
[indistinct chatter]

78
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:47,667
Um, guys, let's go to another place.

79
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:51,254
‪[indistinct]

80
00:02:51,921 --> 00:02:52,797
Huh?

81
00:02:53,882 --> 00:02:55,675
Babe, um, let's go to another place.

82
00:02:55,758 --> 00:02:57,093
Where's Karla?

83
00:02:57,176 --> 00:02:59,304
Uh, somewhere over there
with her friends, maybe.

84
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:00,513
[in English] Let's go.

85
00:03:00,597 --> 00:03:02,557
[in English] Uh, with two boys.

86
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,934
Why did you leave her with strangers?

87
00:03:05,018 --> 00:03:06,644
What if something happens to her?

88
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:08,187
[in English] Why are you so mad?!

89
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:09,814
She's not a child. She can handle herself.

90
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:10,732
[in English] Let's go!

91
00:03:10,815 --> 00:03:12,734
You go ahead. I'll look for Karla.

92
00:03:12,817 --> 00:03:13,985
Gavin, I'm your girlfriend!

93
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:15,361
Karla is my friend!

94
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:17,071
She's my responsibility too!

95
00:03:17,155 --> 00:03:18,823
[heavy music playing]

96
00:03:18,907 --> 00:03:20,533
Gavin!

97
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:22,911
[in English] Cath, you better watch out.

98
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:25,788
Maybe Gavin likes Karla now.

99
00:03:27,081 --> 00:03:28,041
[in English] Shut up.

100
00:03:30,084 --> 00:03:30,960
[music fades]

101
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:32,337
Put that there.

102
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,255
- Yes. [indistinct]
- [indistinct]

103
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:35,924
- Be, one juice.
- Yes, I'll handle it.

104
00:03:36,007 --> 00:03:37,050
Here's the payment.

105
00:03:38,801 --> 00:03:41,387
[sighs] What's happening in our barangay?

106
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:43,014
Earlier, there was a shootout.

107
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:46,726
And now, Ibyang almost had an accident!

108
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:49,604
- [Siony sighs]
- Cita, how's Ibyang?

109
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:52,273
[sighs] Atoy and I went to the hospital.

110
00:03:52,357 --> 00:03:53,900
We're home now.

111
00:03:53,983 --> 00:03:55,902
Ibyang is resting.

112
00:03:55,985 --> 00:03:59,405
I just went out again
because Karla hasn't come home.

113
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:02,951
- [suspicious music playing]
- You know, I didn't see her all day.

114
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:05,370
[in English] Oh? What are you guys
doing outside?!

115
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:07,080
[in English] This is not
the time for gossip.

116
00:04:07,163 --> 00:04:08,373
- [in English] It's dangerous right now.
- Uh…

117
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:09,415
[Nestor, in English] Yes, we know.

118
00:04:09,499 --> 00:04:11,793
[in English] But I was there
when they went, um, ah--

119
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:12,794
[imitates a gun firing sound]

120
00:04:12,877 --> 00:04:14,295
[in English] The house of Paldo!
[imitates a gun firing sound]

121
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:16,714
They shot up Paldo's house.

122
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,383
There, right there.

123
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:20,885
Brother Kurt, have you seen Karla?

124
00:04:20,969 --> 00:04:21,803
[in English] Ah, yes.

125
00:04:21,886 --> 00:04:23,388
[in English] She, uh,
was with Denden and her friends.

126
00:04:23,471 --> 00:04:25,348
[in English] I think they went
to some, uh, disco bar.

127
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:28,851
So don't worry, miss,
Karla is safe with Denden.

128
00:04:28,935 --> 00:04:31,604
[rousing music playing]

129
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:34,691
[suave theme music playing]

130
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:38,111
[motorcycle revving]

131
00:04:38,194 --> 00:04:39,070
[sewing machine whirring]

132
00:04:39,153 --> 00:04:40,029
[scratches]

133
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:40,989
[snipping]

134
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:45,910
[sewing machine clacking]

135
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:47,620
- [gun cocks]
- [gunfire]

136
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:49,289
[gunfire]

137
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:51,582
[clacking]

138
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:53,668
[snipping]

139
00:04:54,752 --> 00:04:56,421
[music swells]

140
00:04:56,504 --> 00:04:59,132
[electronic blipping]

141
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:01,926
- [music fades]
- [indistinct]

142
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:03,678
[Karla] It looks fun inside.

143
00:05:03,761 --> 00:05:05,138
No, it's more fun there.

144
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:07,265
- We're going to a more fun club.
- [sinister music playing]

145
00:05:07,765 --> 00:05:09,058
We're going there.

146
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:10,310
We have more friends there.

147
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,770
- Okay. I'll just tell my friends first.
- No, don't bother.

148
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:13,813
- No, let's go.
- Let's go, come with us.

149
00:05:13,896 --> 00:05:15,440
No, so they'll know where I am.

150
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:16,441
- Hey, hey, hey.
- [boy 1] Get in.

151
00:05:16,524 --> 00:05:17,567
Where are you taking her?

152
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:19,444
- Don't meddle here.
- Gavin.

153
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:21,612
[boy 2] Just leave.

154
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:23,990
Karla is my friend. I'll take her home.
Karla, let's go.

155
00:05:24,073 --> 00:05:25,742
Don't meddle, bro. Don't meddle.

156
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:27,410
- Just leave.
- [Gavin] Karla, come on.

157
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:29,078
- [boy 2] You're annoying.
- [boy 2] Karla is coming with us.

158
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:30,621
- [Gavin] What?
- Don't meddle.

159
00:05:30,705 --> 00:05:31,664
[Karla] Gavin!

160
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:33,124
- [boy 1] Karla is coming with us.
- Bro, bro, relax.

161
00:05:33,207 --> 00:05:35,626
[ominous music playing]

162
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:39,422
- [grunting and groaning]
- [Karla shrieks]

163
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:40,840
Come here! [grunts]

164
00:05:40,923 --> 00:05:41,799
[boy 1] Ouch.

165
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:43,217
- [boy 1 grunts]
- What?! You want to fight?!

166
00:05:43,301 --> 00:05:45,219
- No. Sorry.
- No. Bro, let's go.

167
00:05:45,303 --> 00:05:46,262
- [boy 1] Sorry.
- Oh?

168
00:05:46,345 --> 00:05:47,221
[boy 1 gunts]

169
00:05:47,305 --> 00:05:48,264
Let's go, Karla.

170
00:05:49,307 --> 00:05:50,391
[music concludes]

171
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:53,269
Gavin, thank you.

172
00:05:53,352 --> 00:05:55,772
Why did you go with them?

173
00:05:55,855 --> 00:05:57,231
You don't even know them.

174
00:05:58,066 --> 00:06:00,193
They were nice to me.

175
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:05,615
But when I saw them ganging up on you,
they weren't nice anymore.

176
00:06:05,698 --> 00:06:06,657
- They became enemies.
- [gentle music playing]

177
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:09,702
They're nice to you
because they have other motives.

178
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:11,704
Can you imagine? What if you were drunk?

179
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:13,372
Then you'd have no defense against them.

180
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:15,500
I'm sorry!

181
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:17,627
I didn't know.

182
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:19,170
It's my first time doing things like this.

183
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:23,508
At least, I could tell my problems
to them without judgment.

184
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:26,010
Why tell them?

185
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:27,553
I'm here.

186
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:31,224
[melancholic music playing]

187
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:34,936
Cathy doesn't want me near you, so…

188
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:37,563
Don't worry about Cathy.

189
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:40,650
Before I met her, we were already friends.

190
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:44,112
And no matter what you're going through,
I won't judge you.

191
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:50,493
Anything?

192
00:06:52,578 --> 00:06:53,412
[in English] Promise?

193
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:55,039
[in English] Promise.

194
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:59,127
Even if we're deceiving people?

195
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:02,338
Even if I'm the child of a mistress?

196
00:07:07,093 --> 00:07:10,596
[music swells]

197
00:07:16,727 --> 00:07:19,313
Your own man eluded you?

198
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:21,107
[in English] He knows how you operate.

199
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:23,151
What if he reports to the police?

200
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:25,653
I'm not worried about the police.

201
00:07:25,736 --> 00:07:27,155
[mysterious music playing]

202
00:07:27,238 --> 00:07:29,449
I'm worried he might tell Atoy.

203
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:31,659
[sighs] What about him again?

204
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:36,330
Look. The vehicle Paldo used was Atoy's.

205
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:37,957
I don't know

206
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:40,793
how deep their connection is.

207
00:07:41,627 --> 00:07:45,131
But if he doesn't go to the police,
he might talk to Atoy.

208
00:07:45,214 --> 00:07:47,550
[scoffs, in English] What can Atoy do?

209
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:49,719
[in English] Hon, he's just one man!

210
00:07:49,802 --> 00:07:50,720
[in English] Yes.

211
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,723
He's already ruined
many of our operations.

212
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:56,809
Remember our ivory smuggling
business before?

213
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:00,354
[gunfire blasting]

214
00:08:01,272 --> 00:08:03,983
He's the reason that was exposed.

215
00:08:05,193 --> 00:08:06,360
[in English] Okay. Well, then… [sighs]

216
00:08:06,444 --> 00:08:09,572
[in English] Do something about this Atoy
before anything happens.

217
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:11,574
[Martina sighs]

218
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:13,201
- [Martina] Mmm…
- [music fades]

219
00:08:13,284 --> 00:08:15,036
[Audrey] What will you do to Atoy?

220
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:18,581
[tense music playing]

221
00:08:25,671 --> 00:08:27,882
Are you planning
something bad against Atoy?

222
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:30,718
We were just talking about him.

223
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:32,803
[mysterious music playing]

224
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:35,306
Someone shot people at Mongki's place.

225
00:08:35,389 --> 00:08:37,475
And the vehicle used was Atoy's.

226
00:08:37,558 --> 00:08:39,560
[suspicious music playing]

227
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:42,313
Why would he shoot Mongki?

228
00:08:42,396 --> 00:08:44,357
Not unless Mongki struck first,

229
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,317
and he was just acting in self-defense.

230
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:48,611
Since you and Atoy separated
eight years ago,

231
00:08:48,694 --> 00:08:51,113
you only had a few days with him.

232
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:53,991
[in English] So… [scoffs] you don't
really know him that well.

233
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:55,701
[in English] For all you know,
he's a criminal.

234
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:56,869
[in English] I don't think so.

235
00:08:58,287 --> 00:09:00,540
[sighs] You're just too in love!

236
00:09:00,623 --> 00:09:03,251
[in English] That's why everything
seems so right with this man.

237
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:06,087
Think carefully about who
you let into your life

238
00:09:06,170 --> 00:09:07,713
and into Janine's life.

239
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:10,132
[in English] I may not
know him that well right now.

240
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,635
[in English] But what I do know…

241
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,346
[pensive music playing]

242
00:09:15,429 --> 00:09:18,599
…is that he's nothing like you.

243
00:09:20,851 --> 00:09:22,812
Okay. Then I'm a bad person.

244
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:24,939
But what if he is too?

245
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,318
You still don't know him that well.

246
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:31,862
- [clicks tongue]
- [tense music playing]

247
00:09:31,946 --> 00:09:32,863
[in English] Let's go.

248
00:09:49,547 --> 00:09:50,756
[music fades]

249
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:55,511
So, your real father
is Brother Atoy's father?

250
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:56,470
- [sniffs]
- [in English] That makes him

251
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:57,722
your half-brother.

252
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:01,809
Don't you want that?

253
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:06,272
[in English] Haven't you always looked up
to Brother Atoy as an older brother?

254
00:10:07,898 --> 00:10:10,735
I do want Brother Atoy
to be my real brother.

255
00:10:11,485 --> 00:10:13,988
Just not having different moms,
and he doesn't even know.

256
00:10:14,071 --> 00:10:15,906
[pensive music playing]

257
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:18,576
Mom asked me not to tell him.

258
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,329
That made it harder for me.

259
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:22,955
[mellow music playing]

260
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:24,206
I get you.

261
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:26,626
That's hard because

262
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:28,044
the fact that you know the truth

263
00:10:28,127 --> 00:10:30,338
and you have to act normal.

264
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:31,756
[in English] That's lying itself.

265
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:34,175
I wish I had known earlier,

266
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:38,387
so I could have known him better,
my real father.

267
00:10:39,513 --> 00:10:41,265
That's what I regret.

268
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:44,143
The time we lost.

269
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:46,395
You can still do that.

270
00:10:46,479 --> 00:10:49,732
Not with Sir Delfin,
but with Brother Atoy.

271
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:50,816
[in English] You know what?

272
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,735
[in English] Why not
get to know him better?

273
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:53,944
[in English] Spend time with him.

274
00:10:54,612 --> 00:10:57,740
He's still your brother,
even if you're the only one who knows.

275
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:01,952
And don't think your friends
will judge you just because of that.

276
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:06,248
I'm pretty sure they'll accept you,
no matter what.

277
00:11:07,291 --> 00:11:10,878
[gentle music playing]

278
00:11:10,961 --> 00:11:12,338
Gavin, thank you.

279
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:17,760
I didn't really need alcohol
or to dress like this.

280
00:11:17,843 --> 00:11:19,512
It suits you, though.

281
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:21,472
You could use that for basketball.

282
00:11:21,555 --> 00:11:24,392
[chuckles]

283
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:26,435
There!

284
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:28,813
You're finally smiling.

285
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:30,272
I missed that too.

286
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:36,028
You're beautiful when you smile.

287
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:39,615
- Be quiet now.
- [chuckles]

288
00:11:39,698 --> 00:11:40,533
You're annoying.

289
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:45,746
[music fades]

290
00:11:57,716 --> 00:11:59,301
- Godmother.
- Hmm?

291
00:12:00,594 --> 00:12:01,929
Is Ibyang asleep?

292
00:12:03,639 --> 00:12:05,766
What are you waiting for?
Karla's still not here?

293
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:09,603
Uh, she went out with Denden,
Kurt's godchild.

294
00:12:09,687 --> 00:12:11,689
I tried calling, but I couldn't reach her.

295
00:12:11,772 --> 00:12:14,400
Even Karla's phone is off.

296
00:12:15,401 --> 00:12:16,944
Where did she go?

297
00:12:18,362 --> 00:12:20,906
And I haven't seen Karla for a long time.

298
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:22,741
What's happening to her?

299
00:12:22,825 --> 00:12:28,831
[pensive music playing]

300
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:33,169
[music fades]

301
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:37,298
Psst, hey.

302
00:12:38,757 --> 00:12:40,634
[clicks tongue] Where did you come from?

303
00:12:40,718 --> 00:12:44,096
[pensive music playing]

304
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:46,932
I thought you were with Denden?

305
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:53,063
Uh, Brother Atoy, Denden left,
so I just accompanied Karla.

306
00:12:53,647 --> 00:12:55,024
Where did you go? And why…

307
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:56,817
Why are you dressed like that?

308
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:58,694
It looks like you ran out of fabric.

309
00:12:58,777 --> 00:13:00,404
We have plenty of fabric here.

310
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:05,367
Sister Denden just lent it to me,
and it was a bar.

311
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:06,285
[Atoy, in English] Bar?

312
00:13:06,952 --> 00:13:09,538
[suspicious music playing]

313
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:10,915
[Cita] Uh…

314
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:13,876
Come on. Let's go home.

315
00:13:13,959 --> 00:13:16,003
Come on. You should've at least texted.

316
00:13:16,086 --> 00:13:18,464
There was a shootout.
I didn't know who to call to find you.

317
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:20,090
Come on. Let's go home.

318
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:23,302
Gavin, thank you.

319
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:24,929
[Cita] Let's go.

320
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:30,142
What was the shootout about?

321
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:32,061
- Who caused trouble?
- You don't need to know.

322
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:37,983
Gavin, you have other friends, right?

323
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:42,905
I want you to stay away from Karla.

324
00:13:42,988 --> 00:13:46,659
Brother Atoy, I don't have
bad intentions toward Karla.

325
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:47,576
I know.

326
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:51,580
I don't need to explain myself to you.

327
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,165
Believe me.

328
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:56,502
This is better for her.

329
00:13:58,754 --> 00:14:03,008
And also, do you know
where your father will be tomorrow?

330
00:14:03,884 --> 00:14:07,763
I just need to ask him something.

331
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:11,559
[suave theme music playing]

332
00:14:32,204 --> 00:14:34,665
[music intensifies]

333
00:14:34,748 --> 00:14:35,541
[music fades]

334
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:37,668
Buddy, you can take a break.

335
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:39,253
Perfect. I'm hungry.

336
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:42,548
- Wait. Sir, hold on.
- Sir, sir, sir, sir, just a moment.

337
00:14:42,631 --> 00:14:43,507
Sir.

338
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:44,925
Sir, wait!
Sir, who are you looking for, sir?

339
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:47,595
[tense music playing]

340
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:51,765
[grunting and groaning]

341
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:58,063
[grunts]

342
00:15:06,071 --> 00:15:07,364
[music fades]

343
00:15:07,448 --> 00:15:10,701
[Mongki] We searched all possible
hiding places of Paldo last night, boss.

344
00:15:11,201 --> 00:15:12,453
Nothing.

345
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:15,080
He has no relatives here in Manila.

346
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:17,333
- [ominous music playing]
- [Mongki sighs]

347
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:19,960
Follow him to the province.

348
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:21,754
[sniffs]

349
00:15:24,673 --> 00:15:25,549
Is that the gun?

350
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:28,385
[in English] Yes, boss.

351
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:35,434
[anxious music playing]

352
00:15:42,983 --> 00:15:44,860
[music fades]

353
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:48,447
[tense music playing]

354
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:53,327
[car revving and tires screeching]

355
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:54,912
[crashes]

356
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:58,207
[car revving]

357
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:02,211
[music swells]

358
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:08,801
[phone ringing]

359
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:09,843
[music concludes]

360
00:16:09,927 --> 00:16:11,845
Gavin? How are you?

361
00:16:12,429 --> 00:16:14,139
Ah, your jacket.

362
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:15,516
Just get it at the house, okay.

363
00:16:15,599 --> 00:16:18,185
Um, Karla, just keep it for now.

364
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:22,022
Last night Brother Atoy told me
not to go near you.

365
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:23,816
I'm scared of him. [sighs]

366
00:16:23,899 --> 00:16:26,068
- [gentle music playing]
- Huh? Why?

367
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:28,153
[Gavin] <i>He said it's for your own good.</i>

368
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:29,780
Did I do something wrong?

369
00:16:30,614 --> 00:16:32,616
I didn't abandon you last night.

370
00:16:33,534 --> 00:16:34,493
[in English] Weird.

371
00:16:34,576 --> 00:16:36,245
Brother Atoy isn't usually like that.

372
00:16:36,745 --> 00:16:38,163
What else did he say to you?

373
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:40,916
He's looking for my father.

374
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,167
Do they have an issue?

375
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:43,836
I don't know.

376
00:16:44,336 --> 00:16:46,296
You know, just let Brother Atoy be.

377
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:48,674
He's just intimidating us
because I stayed out late.

378
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:52,136
Gavin, thank you again last night.

379
00:16:52,636 --> 00:16:53,971
- [pleasant music playing]
- I miss bonding with you.

380
00:16:55,472 --> 00:16:56,724
[in English] I missed you too.

381
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:58,142
Next time again, okay.

382
00:17:05,357 --> 00:17:06,567
[music fades]

383
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:08,485
[suspicious music playing]

384
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:09,403
[soft grunt]

385
00:17:09,486 --> 00:17:10,446
Hey!

386
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,783
What are you doing here?

387
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:16,744
Audrey isn't here--

388
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:18,328
Don't meddle here.

389
00:17:19,329 --> 00:17:20,372
Move aside!

390
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:21,790
[tense music playing]

391
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:23,125
Come here.

392
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:25,794
Call the guard. Make Atoy leave.

393
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:26,879
[in English] Yes, ma'am.

394
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:31,008
[music fades]

395
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:33,927
- [horn honks]
- Oh, needle!

396
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:35,471
What-- What is that?!

397
00:17:35,554 --> 00:17:37,598
[pensive music playing]

398
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:41,727
Karla, let's talk.

399
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:44,313
No "good morning" at all?

400
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:47,775
There's nothing good about the morning,
except for those who steal.

401
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:49,777
[in English] So, what?

402
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,153
[in English] Are you trying
to steal my boyfriend?

403
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:53,655
Cathy, Gavin and I are just friends.

404
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:54,948
I won't steal him from you.

405
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:56,950
[in English] Oh, please, Karla!

406
00:17:57,534 --> 00:18:00,412
You really think I don't notice
the way you look at him?

407
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,248
That you're not really happy
that we became a couple.

408
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:05,334
I don't know what you're saying.

409
00:18:05,417 --> 00:18:07,628
[in English] Of course,
you're going to deny it.

410
00:18:07,711 --> 00:18:10,214
[in English] But actions
speak louder than words, Karla.

411
00:18:10,297 --> 00:18:12,591
That's why you acted
like a damsel in distress last night,

412
00:18:12,674 --> 00:18:15,677
so Gavin would be forced
to choose you over me.

413
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:18,847
I didn't force him
to be with me last night.

414
00:18:18,931 --> 00:18:19,765
You stay there!

415
00:18:19,848 --> 00:18:21,517
[in English] I'm not finished yet!

416
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,893
Let me go!

417
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:25,437
Wow, an early confrontation.

418
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:26,980
- Yes.
- Hey, let's take a video.

419
00:18:27,064 --> 00:18:29,066
- Hurry, hurry, girl.
- [indistinct]

420
00:18:29,149 --> 00:18:30,400
[phone blips]

421
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:31,652
[suspicious music playing]

422
00:18:31,735 --> 00:18:34,029
Didn't you talk to Atoy?

423
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:36,323
He left. I thought he was going to you.

424
00:18:36,406 --> 00:18:38,408
Ah, he texted me last night.

425
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:40,661
He told us to come here.

426
00:18:40,744 --> 00:18:42,496
So why did he leave?

427
00:18:42,996 --> 00:18:45,499
Um, maybe he just bought something.

428
00:18:45,582 --> 00:18:47,167
Sit down first while waiting.

429
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:49,795
- [sighs]
- Ah, Mommy, I'll just go to the CR.

430
00:18:49,878 --> 00:18:51,130
- I need to pee.
- Okay.

431
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:52,506
I'll go with you.

432
00:18:52,589 --> 00:18:55,175
Ah, no. It's fine. I know where it is.

433
00:18:55,259 --> 00:18:56,218
All right.

434
00:18:59,555 --> 00:19:01,598
Audrey, sit down.

435
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:03,183
- Okay, thank you.
- [Emerson] Miss.

436
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:04,935
- Oh?
- Where's Atoy?

437
00:19:05,435 --> 00:19:08,188
He left. Didn't say where he was going.

438
00:19:09,773 --> 00:19:11,316
Oh, no. [clicks tongue]

439
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,610
I didn't catch him.
Who knows what he'll do.

440
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:16,196
- What?
- What do you mean?

441
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,948
Is he okay?

442
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:21,535
Audrey, uh, what are you doing here?

443
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:23,704
He told me and Janine to come here.

444
00:19:23,787 --> 00:19:27,166
He said we'd have lunch out,
but he's not here.

445
00:19:27,249 --> 00:19:29,084
Ah, what's happening, Emerson?

446
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:31,587
[tense music playing]

447
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:33,213
Ah, ah-- Audrey…

448
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:36,383
[inhales]

449
00:19:36,466 --> 00:19:38,677
Didn't Atoy tell you? [inhales]

450
00:19:40,387 --> 00:19:42,931
He knows who killed his father.

451
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:45,350
- [gasps]
- [music fades]

452
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:48,562
- Your brother, Red.
- [Cita gasps]

453
00:19:48,645 --> 00:19:50,981
[intense music playing]

454
00:19:51,064 --> 00:19:52,149
[Emerson] Yes.

455
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:54,526
He wanted to go after Red last night, but…

456
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:56,987
we stopped him.

457
00:19:58,322 --> 00:19:59,573
But now it looks like we can't anymore.

458
00:19:59,656 --> 00:20:00,490
[music fades]

459
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:08,498
This is great.

460
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:10,209
[chuckles] Of course, boss.

461
00:20:10,709 --> 00:20:11,835
I have good news, boss.

462
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:12,836
Hmm?

463
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:15,339
Remember Sister Norma,
who suddenly disappeared?

464
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:18,175
My guy found out she moved to the province

465
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:20,928
and came to Manila a week ago!

466
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:23,180
She stayed with relatives.

467
00:20:23,263 --> 00:20:24,556
[mysterious music playing]

468
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,515
You found her?

469
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:27,643
Roger is looking for her.

470
00:20:27,726 --> 00:20:29,144
He'll update me later.

471
00:20:29,937 --> 00:20:32,940
[energetic rock music playing]

472
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:40,197
- [Red sighs]
- [music fades]

473
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,198
[henchman] Hey!

474
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:42,908
What are you doing here?!

475
00:20:42,991 --> 00:20:45,661
[groaning]

476
00:20:47,037 --> 00:20:48,330
[Mongki] Boss, boss, let's go!

477
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:26,201
[grunting and groaning]

478
00:21:30,956 --> 00:21:32,791
[in English] Martina, what's happening?

479
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:34,543
- [in English] Dad--
- Is there a shootout?

480
00:21:34,626 --> 00:21:35,460
[in English] We have a problem.

481
00:21:35,544 --> 00:21:37,254
[in English] Atoy is here.
And I think he's after Red!

482
00:21:39,214 --> 00:21:43,176
- [line ringing]
- [sighs]

483
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,594
[softly, in English]
Pick up, pick up, pick up.

484
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:51,059
- [line rings]
- [phone ringing]

485
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:52,477
[in English] Hello, Audrey.

486
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:56,064
Atoy is here at the trucking compound.

487
00:21:56,148 --> 00:21:57,858
Do you know why he's here?

488
00:21:57,941 --> 00:21:59,067
[in English] What?

489
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:00,819
Ah, Dad, is Red there?

490
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:03,989
[sighs] They can't meet.

491
00:22:04,072 --> 00:22:06,241
He's the one Atoy is looking for here.

492
00:22:06,950 --> 00:22:11,997
Dad, Red killed Atoy's father.

493
00:22:12,789 --> 00:22:14,082
That's why he's there,

494
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:16,626
to go after Red.

495
00:22:17,294 --> 00:22:18,211
[in English] Sir.

496
00:22:18,712 --> 00:22:20,339
Sir Red is fighting with someone.

497
00:22:20,839 --> 00:22:23,342
[employee] They're shooting
at each other at the firing range.

498
00:22:23,425 --> 00:22:26,011
Dad, stop Atoy! [gasps]

499
00:22:26,094 --> 00:22:29,306
[employee] Some of our guards
are already dead.

500
00:22:29,389 --> 00:22:30,974
What the-- Dad.

501
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:32,559
- [in English] Come on, let's go. Let's go.
- [in English] Let's go.

502
00:22:32,642 --> 00:22:34,227
[gasps] Um, Miss Cita,

503
00:22:34,311 --> 00:22:35,729
can I leave Janine with you for now?

504
00:22:35,812 --> 00:22:37,314
I'll just go to Atoy, okay?

505
00:22:37,397 --> 00:22:38,774
- Audrey…
- You can--

506
00:22:38,857 --> 00:22:40,817
Atoy has no allies at your place.

507
00:22:40,901 --> 00:22:42,402
Don't abandon him, okay?

508
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:44,321
[tense music playing]

509
00:22:44,404 --> 00:22:46,823
- [Emerson mutters]
- [Audrey gasps]

510
00:22:47,491 --> 00:22:49,910
[sighs] My God.

511
00:22:51,036 --> 00:22:52,162
Miss…

512
00:22:53,163 --> 00:22:55,207
to be honest, I don't think that…

513
00:22:56,124 --> 00:22:59,336
Eh, I'm not worried
that Atoy has no allies there.

514
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:02,089
With how furious Atoy is,

515
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:04,591
some innocent lives
might get entangled in it too.

516
00:23:05,383 --> 00:23:06,510
My God. [gasps]

517
00:23:07,427 --> 00:23:09,805
[gasping]

518
00:23:12,891 --> 00:23:14,184
My God.

519
00:23:16,019 --> 00:23:18,271
- [growls]
- [gunshots]

520
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:20,982
[growls]

521
00:23:21,066 --> 00:23:22,442
[grunts]

522
00:23:22,526 --> 00:23:24,152
[grunting and groaning]

523
00:23:24,820 --> 00:23:26,279
[growls]

524
00:23:26,363 --> 00:23:30,117
[grunting and groaning]

525
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,409
[tense music playing]

526
00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:33,161
[grunts]

527
00:23:34,996 --> 00:23:37,040
[grunts]

528
00:23:37,124 --> 00:23:39,918
[grunting and groaning]

529
00:23:40,502 --> 00:23:41,711
You animal.

530
00:23:41,795 --> 00:23:43,296
I know the truth now.

531
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:45,465
You killed my father!

532
00:23:45,549 --> 00:23:48,135
[rousing music playing]

533
00:23:48,718 --> 00:23:51,680
You know, this is what
should be done to women

534
00:23:51,763 --> 00:23:53,348
- who are sluts like you!
- [shrieks, grunting]

535
00:23:53,431 --> 00:23:54,307
[Karla] What is this?!

536
00:23:54,391 --> 00:23:55,433
[clamoring]

537
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:57,269
[Karla] Stop it, Cathy!

538
00:23:57,352 --> 00:23:58,395
- [grunts]
- [Karla] What?!

539
00:23:58,478 --> 00:24:00,105
[soft rock music playing]

540
00:24:00,188 --> 00:24:01,022
[Cathy grunts]

541
00:24:02,023 --> 00:24:03,066
[grunting]

542
00:24:03,150 --> 00:24:05,485
That's Karla! Oh!

543
00:24:05,569 --> 00:24:06,611
- Oh, no, there she is.
- [shrieks]

544
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:08,113
- Hurry, let's go to her!
- [gasping]

545
00:24:08,196 --> 00:24:09,281
[clamoring]

546
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:11,491
[Karla] Let me go!

547
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:13,493
[clamoring]

548
00:24:13,577 --> 00:24:15,120
[Jona] Stop it, stop it!

549
00:24:15,203 --> 00:24:16,163
[grunts]

550
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:20,208
[grunting and groaning]

551
00:24:22,919 --> 00:24:24,254
My father did nothing wrong to you.

552
00:24:24,337 --> 00:24:26,214
I will kill you!

553
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:30,385
[growls and grunts]

554
00:24:30,468 --> 00:24:33,180
[tense music playing]

555
00:24:33,263 --> 00:24:35,098
- You're really an animal!
- [Dmitri] Red!

556
00:24:35,182 --> 00:24:36,892
- [growls]
- [Martina, in English] Stop him!

557
00:24:36,975 --> 00:24:38,518
[Martina, in English] Stop it, Dad! Dad!

558
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:39,686
- [groaning]
- [Martina, in English] Oh my God, Red!

559
00:24:39,769 --> 00:24:41,646
- [growling]
- [Martina gasps]

560
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:43,940
- [groans]
- [shrieks]

561
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:44,983
[growls]

562
00:24:45,066 --> 00:24:46,401
Stop hurting my child!

563
00:24:46,484 --> 00:24:49,070
[in English] Stay away
from my husband! [gasps]

564
00:24:49,154 --> 00:24:50,071
[in English] Hon, get up.

565
00:24:50,655 --> 00:24:53,241
[in English] Get up, hon! Please, please!

566
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:54,367
- [in English] Get up.
- [Red grunts]

567
00:24:56,203 --> 00:24:58,622
[pensive music playing]

568
00:25:00,248 --> 00:25:02,417
Your son killed my father.

569
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:04,628
[music swells]

570
00:25:04,711 --> 00:25:06,755
My father had cancer then.

571
00:25:08,089 --> 00:25:10,592
But I wish he had just let my father live,

572
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:12,594
so I could have spent more time with him.

573
00:25:14,054 --> 00:25:17,641
[in English] I'm sorry,
but you have to stop this.

574
00:25:19,267 --> 00:25:22,187
You can't get your father back
if you kill Red.

575
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:25,732
That's not what I want. [inhales]

576
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,026
What I want…

577
00:25:28,109 --> 00:25:31,655
[gasps]

578
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:33,865
What I want is revenge.

579
00:25:35,575 --> 00:25:39,037
He didn't just take a life, he took time.

580
00:25:39,120 --> 00:25:41,206
Time I could have spent with my father.

581
00:25:41,289 --> 00:25:42,958
So, I will kill your son.

582
00:25:45,961 --> 00:25:47,504
[scoffs, gasps]

583
00:25:48,004 --> 00:25:50,423
If you were in my position, huh?

584
00:25:50,924 --> 00:25:51,800
[scoffs]

585
00:25:51,883 --> 00:25:52,926
What would you do?

586
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:55,303
What?

587
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:00,225
I would kill too.

588
00:26:02,644 --> 00:26:04,145
[in English] But he's still my son.

589
00:26:06,106 --> 00:26:08,441
[in English] It's my duty to protect him.

590
00:26:10,402 --> 00:26:13,071
[in English] We do
what we have to do for family.

591
00:26:13,655 --> 00:26:14,698
[scoffs]

592
00:26:14,781 --> 00:26:15,782
[in English] Family?

593
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:18,326
Don't worry.

594
00:26:18,410 --> 00:26:19,160
‪[gasps]

595
00:26:19,244 --> 00:26:20,787
I won't involve you.

596
00:26:20,870 --> 00:26:22,205
[music swells]

597
00:26:22,289 --> 00:26:23,331
[sharp exhale]

598
00:26:23,415 --> 00:26:27,335
But your son, I will kill him.
[sharp exhale]

599
00:26:27,961 --> 00:26:29,587
[music fades]

600
00:26:30,588 --> 00:26:33,216
[screams]

601
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:36,553
[tense music playing]

602
00:26:37,137 --> 00:26:38,471
[gasps]

603
00:26:41,975 --> 00:26:44,352
[electronic blipping]

604
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:48,064
[tense music playing]

605
00:26:52,277 --> 00:26:53,236
- [Ibyang] Tatoy.
- [Janine] Daddy?

606
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:54,696
[Cita] What happened?

607
00:26:54,779 --> 00:26:56,990
What happened to your hand?

608
00:26:57,657 --> 00:26:59,451
- Is that blood?
- It's nothing.

609
00:26:59,534 --> 00:27:00,785
[Gavin] <i>He shot my grandfather.</i>

610
00:27:00,869 --> 00:27:02,329
He beat up my father!

611
00:27:02,412 --> 00:27:04,497
Your father deserved it!

612
00:27:04,581 --> 00:27:07,459
He killed Sir Delfin,
Brother Atoy's and my dad!

613
00:27:07,542 --> 00:27:10,253
What evidence does your brother
have to accuse him, huh?

614
00:27:10,337 --> 00:27:12,380
He's just like your father.
They're both pretenders!

615
00:27:12,464 --> 00:27:13,882
What you're saying is foul!

616
00:27:14,466 --> 00:27:17,052
I pity you.
I know you're a good kid.

617
00:27:17,135 --> 00:27:20,305
You're just surrounded by liars.

618
00:27:20,388 --> 00:27:21,973
You're the ones who are pitiful!

619
00:27:22,057 --> 00:27:23,641
There are more liars around you!

620
00:27:23,725 --> 00:27:25,060
Why don't you ask Karla?!

621
00:27:25,935 --> 00:27:28,063
What? What about Karla?

622
00:27:28,146 --> 00:27:28,980
[Atoy] What is that?

623
00:27:29,064 --> 00:27:30,231
Are you having something sewn?

624
00:27:30,315 --> 00:27:32,692
‪UP NEXT

625
00:27:33,568 --> 00:27:34,444
[woman shrieks] Hey!

626
00:27:34,527 --> 00:27:36,237
[shrieking]

627
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:37,530
Did Red send you, huh?

628
00:27:38,490 --> 00:27:40,575
- Who sent you?
- Help, help!

629
00:27:41,326 --> 00:27:44,579
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

630
00:27:44,662 --> 00:27:45,747
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

631
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:47,457
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
